{"name":"In the Red","hex":"#ff2233","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"in the red","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Prepositional phrase","definitions":["Having net losses; in debt."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/in_the_red"}],"entries":[{"title":"In the Red (novel)","blocks":[{"text":"In the Red is a 1989 black comedy-crime novel by Mark Tavener, featuring fictional BBC Reporter George Cragge and fictional Police Officer Frank Jefferson, investigating a series of murders of London bank managers, a small political party contesting a by-election, and a plan to overthrow the Director-General of the BBC."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/6/65/BBCBookInTheRedCover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/In_the_Red_(novel)"},{"title":"Live with Yourself!","blocks":[{"text":"Live with Yourself! (LWY) is a science fiction comedy webtoon series written and drawn by Andrew \"Shen\" Tsyaston and David J. Catman. Initially created by the former before passing creative control to the latter, it follows computer support worker Todd as he is split into four versions of himself from different times following a mad science experiment gone-wrong, who he becomes roommates with, his three older selves raising his younger self while dealing with both slice-of-life shenanigans and a serialised plot involving a future time civil war."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Live_with_Yourself!"},{"title":"In the Red (radio series)","blocks":[{"text":"In the Red is the first in a sequence of four black comedy-crime drama series created for BBC Radio 4 by Mark Tavener featuring Michael Williams as BBC Reporter George Cragge and Barry Foster as Police Superintendent Frank Jefferson."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/e/e6/BBCInTheRed.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/In_the_Red_(radio_series)"},{"title":"Red","blocks":[{"text":"Red is the color at the long wavelength end of the visible spectrum of light, next to orange and opposite violet. It has a dominant wavelength of approximately 625–750 nanometers. It is a primary color in the RGB color model and a secondary color in the CMYK color model, and is the complementary color of cyan. Reds range from the brilliant yellow-tinged scarlet and vermillion to bluish-red crimson, and vary in shade from the pale red pink to the dark red burgundy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg/330px-Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/da/Cardinal.jpg/500px-Cardinal.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/da/Cardinal.jpg/500px-Cardinal.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACardinal.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bb/Cardinal_Th%C3%A9odore_Adrien_Sarr_2.JPG/500px-Cardinal_Th%C3%A9odore_Adrien_Sarr_2.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bb/Cardinal_Th%C3%A9odore_Adrien_Sarr_2.JPG/500px-Cardinal_Th%C3%A9odore_Adrien_Sarr_2.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACardinal_Th%C3%A9odore_Adrien_Sarr_2.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3d/Magdalena_Frackowiak.jpg/500px-Magdalena_Frackowiak.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src